# Make the Open Graph image and the HTML shell that carries it

## Step

Render `assets/ratstack-logo.svg` into a 1200 by 630 PNG for Open Graph (charcoal `#262829` background, mark centered with room around it, "ratstack.sh" set small under it in the cream `#FAF5E9`), plus a 512 and a 32 pixel favicon, into `apps/mischief/public/`. Use ImageMagick or resvg locally; keep the SVG as the source and record the exact command so it can be re-run. Then specify the HTML shell the Worker returns when `Accept` prefers `text/html`: a single template with `<title>`, `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image` (absolute URL), `og:url`, `twitter:card` `summary_large_image`, and the plain-text body inside `<pre>`. Check the result with a local unfurl preview (`curl -H 'Accept: text/html'` and an OG debugger once deployed).

Resolved when the PNGs exist under `apps/mischief/public/`, the render command is recorded here, and the template is written down for the prototype step to use.
